 ## Background
 
-Dual Contouring was introduced by Ju et al. in 2002 as "Hermite Dual Contouring" [S2]. It was later extended to Signed Distance Fields by Carrera et al. in 2026 [S2]. The method is used in various graphics applications requiring high-quality isosurface extraction, such as medical imaging and CAD [S1, S2, S3]. Implementations include `IsosurfaceExtraction` (heckj), `isoext` (GuangyanCai), and `isomesh` (narnia-ai-mason) [S1, S2, S3].
